###
# TP3 - Auth + listas/favoritos autenticados
# Requisito: PostgreSQL arriba (docker compose up -d) y app en http://localhost:8080
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) REGISTRO Y LOGIN
###

### Registro -> 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/registro
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "persona@example.com",
  "password": "secreta123"
}

### Registro duplicado -> 409 Conflict
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/registro
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "persona@example.com",
  "password": "secreta123"
}

### Login ok -> 200 (copiar el token de la respuesta)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "persona@example.com",
  "password": "secreta123"
}

### Login mal -> 401 Unauthorized
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "persona@example.com",
  "password": "incorrecta99"
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2) USAR EL TOKEN (reemplazar <TOKEN> con el de la respuesta del login)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Listar listas SIN token -> 401 Unauthorized
GET http://localhost:8080/api/listas
Accept: application/json

### Crear lista (dueño = usuario del token) -> 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/listas
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>

{
  "nombre": "Regalos"
}

### Listar mis listas -> 200 (solo las mías)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/listas
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>

### Obtener mi lista -> 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/listas/1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>

### Obtener lista ajena -> 403 Forbidden (con token de otro usuario)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/listas/2
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_OTRO_USUARIO>

### Salud (público, para despliegue) -> 200
GET http://localhost:8080/health
Accept: application/json
